---
description:
  Verifies that long plain-text and markdown node/edge labels still auto-wrap
  onto multiple lines when markdownAutoWrap is true even though htmlLabels is
  false (non-HTML/SVG text labels). Split from a single upstream test that
  rendered three config variants side by side into this standalone fixture.
config:
  layout: layered
  markdownAutoWrap: true
  htmlLabels: false
title: "Testing with {\"markdownAutoWrap\":true,\"htmlLabels\":false}"
copyOf: flowchart/nightly-check/v2/06-should-wrap-edge-labels-markdownautowrap-true-htmllabels-false.mmd
---
flowchart TD
    A["This is a really long line of plain text that will autowrap and support \n newlines too."]
    B["`This is a really long line of **markdown** text that will autowrap, unless markdownAutoWrap:false is set.`"]
    A -- "Plain text **labels** in flowcharts will autowrap,like node labels. \n Newline characters work too." --> B
    B -- "`**Markdown** edge labels will autowrap, unless markdownAutoWrap: false is set`" --> C
